            <ArticleTitle>Headache and sensation seeking.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>615-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>According to the cognitive theory of sensation seeking, headache sufferers were predicted to score lower than controls on Zuckerman's Sensation Seeking Scale. 26 subjects who experienced chronic headaches scored significantly lower than a group of 26 controls. The relationships between the Sensation Seeking Scale and a number of personality tests are described. Replication of the findings on this scale with headache patients is encouraged as well as exploration of other personality dimensions which show significant relations with sensation seeking.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
